#Burndown charts

        What:
        Burndown Chart is a visual chart that shows the remaining work in a Sprint over time.

        Purpose:

        Track Sprint progress
        See remaining work
        Identify whether the team is on track
        Identify delays or scope changes

        Example:
        Sprint starts with 40 Story Points → work gets completed → remaining points decrease toward 0.

        Important:

        X-axis: Time / Sprint days
        Y-axis: Remaining work (usually Story Points or tasks)

        Interview Answer:

        "A Burndown Chart shows the amount of remaining work against the time remaining in a Sprint. It helps the team track Sprint progress and identify whether they are on track to achieve the Sprint Goal."